  "foaf:name": "Cross sector collaboration grows circular economy",
  "sdo:name": "Cross sector collaboration grows circular economy",
  "sdo:description": "Australia has a waste problem, with the highest per capita material footprint in the world, the third lowest rate of manufacturing self-sufficiency in the OECD and a circular economy that is half the global average. Circular economy is an economic model that aims to retain the value of circulating resources, products, parts and materials through a system that allows for renewability, long life, optimal (re)use, refurbishment, remanufacturing, recycling and biodegradation. Circularity is based on three integrated principles: designing out waste and pollution; keeping products and materials in use; and regenerating natural systems. The FRDC Circular Economy project uses cross-sector, cross-industry and transnational initiatives to identify circular opportunities, develop stakeholders’ circular capacity and capability; and showcase success stories that together will increase adoption of circularity throughout Australian fishing and aquaculture and improve ocean outcomes.",
